&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;hover&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;:)&lt;/span&gt; 00111010&lt;br /&gt;
00101001&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;http://scp-wiki.wdfiles.com/local--files/aiad-homescreen/crom_turntr.png&quot; style=&quot;margin-left: 20px;&quot; width=&quot;75px&quot; alt=&quot;crom_turntr.png&quot; class=&quot;image&quot; /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span&gt;Fun&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;AIAD is supposed to be fun. It can be dramatic. It can be tense. If done correctly, it can even be scary. But mostly it&#039;s meant to be a way of doing something different in the SCPverse that isn&#039;t necessarily focused on humans. Let your imagination go wild.&lt;/p&gt;
